WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:04.000
-Rachel Zegler,
welcome to our show.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.100
We are big fans of yours
here at the show,

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.434
so thank you so much
for coming on.

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:08.868
I appreciate this.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:08.868 --> 00:00:11.634
I'm so -- I can't even.
This is crazy.

00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:12.868
-Alright, good, good.
I'm excited.

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:14.834
I have things I want
to ask about you.

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:18.067
One is your name -- Rachel.
-Yes.

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:21.133
-You got this -- You got your
name from someone very famous.

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:23.300
And am I right?
-You are correct.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.434
I was named after
Rachel Green from "Friends."

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:27.701
-Okay, good. Alright.
That is real?

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:29.601
-That is real.
That is a real fact.

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:31.801
And everybody --
Nobody ever believes me

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:34.133
because they think
that there's no way

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.367
I'm young enough
to be named after "Friends."

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:37.534
But --
-No, you were.

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:38.801
-But I am, yeah.

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:40.701
My mom -- They were
going to name me Catherine,

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:42.734
but my older sister's
Jacqueline, and they thought

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:45.100
that might be too confusing
for babies to figure out.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.634
-Yeah. Catherine and Jacqueline.
Yeah.

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:49.801
-Yeah. And, so, yeah,
my mom loved the way it sounded

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:51.701
on "Friends"
for Jennifer Aniston,

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:53.434
and then that was my name.

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:55.834
-I mean, that's a perfect
person to be named --

00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:57.934
We love -- Who doesn't love
Jennifer Aniston or Rachel?

00:00:57.934 --> 00:00:59.167
-I love Jennifer.

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:00.901
-You could have been
named after the hairstyle.

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:04.434
-I could have been Ross.
-You could have been Ross.

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:05.801
-Who knows?
-You could have been Ross.

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:07.033
Yeah, alright.
-All right, why not, right?

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.100
-Ross Zegler's got a good name
to it, as well.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.200
-Yeah, right?

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.501
-Well, if you want to have
a brother...

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:13.834
I want to talk to you
about this,

00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:15.767
because I know you're a big --
You're a big Swiftie.

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:17.167
-Yes.
-And you were at the...

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.467
I mean, how cool are you?

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:21.667
-She looks very sad,

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:24.200
but that was just
because I had food poisoning.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.567
-No.
-I did.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:26.834
-You did not.
-I did.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:28.934
You still went to the show.
-Oh, I would not have --

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.901
I sold my kidney to be there.

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:32.033
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:34.167
-You love her that much?
-I love her so much.

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:35.567
-Back-in-the-day Swiftie?
-Yeah.

00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:37.534
From self-titled album,

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:39.367
which we're still waiting
for the re-record of.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.868
See? I found my people
in the audience.

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:44.200
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.467
But do you -- Are you
one of those people

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:46.767
at the concerts that yell out,

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:48.267
"Oh, the next song
is going to be this or..."

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:50.767
-Oh, I knew the set list,
I know the callbacks,

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:52.267
and I was waiting
for the secret songs.

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:53.467
-Secret songs.
-Yeah.

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:54.601
-My best friend, Brenna,

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:56.701
had gone in Atlanta,
before the MetLife show,

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:57.834
and I went to MetLife Night 1.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:58.901
And she said --
-Whoo!

00:01:58.901 --> 00:02:00.100
-Thank you.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.934
And she said to my older sister,
Jacqueline,

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:03.534
who I took to the show
with me --

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:04.934
She was like, "Jacqueline,

00:02:04.934 --> 00:02:08.300
if they play 'Getaway Car'
or 'Maroon,'

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:10.234
she's on crisis watch."

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:12.701
Not only did she play
"Getaway Car,"

00:02:12.701 --> 00:02:14.934
she also played "Maroon."

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.534
I was having a mental breakdown
in the audience

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:19.234
at MetLife Stadium.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:20.367
-I love it.

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:22.100
-Yeah.
And then Ice Spice came out.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.167
And I kept making the joke --
-That's right.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:25.868
-Exactly.
-I remember that.

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:27.234
-Yeah.
-That was a big deal.

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:29.400
-I was making a joke all night
to the girls behind me.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.067
Wherever they are,
they can attest to it.

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:33.200
I kept making the joke that
Ice Spice was going to come out,

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.100
not knowing anything about
that actually happening,

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.834
and then it happened.

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:39.467
-Wow. So you should
play the lottery that night.

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:40.901
-Yeah.
-Anything you did came true.

00:02:40.901 --> 00:02:44.667
-My Swiftie manifestation
says "Reputation TV" is coming.

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:46.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:48.300
-Okay.
-Thank you.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.267
-Right now, let's talk
about "Hunger Games," okay?

00:02:50.267 --> 00:02:53.100
"The Ballad of Songbirds --"
Let's focus.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.567
The "Ballad of Songbirds
and Snakes."

00:02:54.567 --> 00:02:55.667
-Yes.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.167
-By the way, your character,

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:58.634
Lucy Gray,
sings a lot in the film.

00:02:58.634 --> 00:03:00.200
-Yes, she does.
-Which is great.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.801
Which you did live on set.
-I did, yeah.

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:04.133
-You can do it.
You know how to do it.

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:05.934
I mean, I was reading somewhere,

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:07.834
there was, like, inspirations
of Dolly Parton in there.

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:09.334
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:13.400
Well, it's -- She's a very --
She's a country, folksy singer.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.434
And, so, Suzanne Collins,
who wrote the book --

00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:17.234
she used to be
a country-music deejay.

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:18.267
So she had this, like --
-Oh!

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:20.000
-Yeah. And it's like
she has such

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.033
a deep knowledge
of that whole world,

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:24.767
which I really didn't know
too much about.

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:26.100
-I didn't know
she was a country deejay.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.667
-I didn't either.
-That's fascinating.

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:31.567
-Yeah. And so she's obsessed
with Dolly Parton, Patsy Cline,

00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:34.667
and then we kind of
based her voice off of that.

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:35.834
-How cool.
-Yeah.

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:38.033
-Well, the soundtrack --
it comes out this Friday,

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.300
as well, with you
are featured on it.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.467
-Yeah.

00:03:40.467 --> 00:03:43.033
-And Olivia Rodrigo
is featured on the album.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:44.133
-Yeah.

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:45.234
So everyone's
talking about this.

00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:46.501
-Yeah.

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:47.767
-It's already got over
a million streams already.

00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:49.734
It's just crushing.
Congratulations.

00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:50.834
-Thank you.

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:53.234
-And you accidentally
started a rumor,

00:03:53.234 --> 00:03:54.968
and I thought tonight
would be the perfect night

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.334
for you to clear up this rumor.

00:03:56.334 --> 00:03:58.834
-It's time to address it.
Oh, my goodness.

00:03:58.834 --> 00:04:01.133
Yeah, I accidentally
started a rumor

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:02.801
that Nicki Minaj
was on the album

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:03.801
for "The Hunger Games:

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:05.133
The Ballad
of Songbirds and Snakes."

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.400
-That is not true.
-It's not true. She's not.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:10.200
She's releasing her album
on Friday, I believe.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.634
But it was one of those things

00:04:11.634 --> 00:04:17.033
where there's a character
named Barb Azure in the movie.

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:18.667
And the actress who plays
Barb Azure

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:19.901
has a great sense of humor.

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:22.133
Her name is Honor Gillies.
She's so fantastic.

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:24.200
And posted a video
of Nicki Minaj saying,

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:27.033
"Calling all Barbs"
when she got cast.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:31.133
And her character plays
the stand-up bass in the movie.

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:35.100
So, obviously, I commented,
"Slapping that super bass,"

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.133
as you would.

00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:39.367
-Yeah.
-Now, the Barbs got me good.

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:41.634
They were screen-shotting
those comments,

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:43.467
posting them
all over social media,

00:04:43.467 --> 00:04:45.400
being like,
"What is mother doing?

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:48.934
They are very, very, very
dedicated and amazing.

00:04:48.934 --> 00:04:50.434
I am a Barb.
I love Nicki.

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:52.367
-Yeah.
-But she's not on the album.

00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:54.033
But she started playing into it.

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:57.133
She posted a TikTok
with "The Hanging Tree" song,

00:04:57.133 --> 00:05:00.167
saying like, "I have something
coming out November 17th."

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:02.400
Like, she knew what
she was doing.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.801
I had no idea what I was doing.
-No idea what she was doing.

00:05:04.801 --> 00:05:06.667
No, no. You were just being you
and you go, "I didn't know.

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:07.868
I'd even start this rumor."

00:05:07.868 --> 00:05:10.033
-And I didn't know if she
was on the soundtrack,

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:13.000
so I was just
kind of like, "Okay."

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.033
-And she's not.
-And she's not.

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:15.067
-Okay, good.
I'm glad you said it.

00:05:15.067 --> 00:05:17.434
-Just me.
-Yeah. No, good. I'm glad.

00:05:17.434 --> 00:05:18.467
It's you and Olivia Rodrigo.
-Yeah.

00:05:18.467 --> 00:05:19.467
-We're happy.
-Yeah.

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:20.801
-Okay, yeah, we're good.
-Thanks.

00:05:20.801 --> 00:05:23.067
-Do we set -- How do we set up
the movie "Hunger Games"?

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:27.067
This is pre-Katniss.
-Set 64 years in the past.

00:05:27.067 --> 00:05:29.634
It's been 10 years
since the districts

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:32.367
and The Capitol
have, like, gone to war.

00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:34.634
And the Hunger Games have been
going on for 10 years.

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.667
-It's a giant,
giant, giant movie.

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:40.000
And I would suggest go see it
in IMAX because it's just a lot.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.300
-And we did film it for IMAX.
It's the craziest experience.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.968
-Enjoy it.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:44.968 --> 00:05:47.467
Here's Rachel Zegler
in "The Hunger Games:

00:05:47.467 --> 00:05:49.801
The Ballad of Songbirds
and Snakes."

00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:51.000
Take a look.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.968
-♪ This world, it's dark ♪

00:05:52.968 --> 00:05:55.400
♪ This world, it's scary ♪

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:59.534
♪ I've taken some,
and so no wonder I'm weary ♪

00:05:59.534 --> 00:06:01.767
♪ It's why ♪

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:03.467
♪ I need you ♪

00:06:03.467 --> 00:06:11.234
♪ You're as pure as
the driven snow ♪

00:06:11.234 --> 00:06:12.934
[ Vocalizing ]

00:06:19.901 --> 00:06:25.701
♪♪

00:06:25.701 --> 00:06:28.067
-Whoo!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:28.067 --> 00:06:29.734
Rachel Zegler!

00:06:29.734 --> 00:06:31.167
"The Hunger Games:

00:06:31.167 --> 00:06:33.234
The Ballad of
Songbirds and Snakes"

00:06:33.234 --> 00:06:36.300
is in theaters
and IMAX this Friday.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.567
Hi to Fiona?
-Hi to Fiona.

00:06:38.567 --> 00:06:40.000
-Hi to Fiona.
-Hi, Fiona!

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.534
We'll be right back
with Tariq Trotter, everybody.

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:42.801
Stick around.

